  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q07-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The coefficients of $x^4$ and $x^3$ in the expansion of $(a+x)^5$ are in the ratio $1:4$. Find the value of $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}[x^4](a+x)^5&=\\binom{5}{4}a=5a\\\\{}[x^3](a+x)^5&=\\binom{5}{3}a^2=10a^2\\end{align*}$$\nThe stated ratio requires nonzero coefficients, so $a\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{10a^2}{5a}&=4\\\\2a&=4\\\\a&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
